From 7e0cde3ec7d457fec4f7c1f1f43293477a16c854 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:38:47 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 wave 18f: expose the password leak detection
 preference

Add get/set for Chromium's own profile.password_manager_leak_detection pref (default on, as in Chrome). With it on, ChromePasswordManagerClient's LeakDetectionDelegate sends a submitted sign-in's credential check to Google; off, no check is started. Get reports whether enterprise policy manages the pref (Set is then invalid_state); off-the-record profiles never run leak checks and are rejected. ABI 1.35 / bridge 0.37.0 (password_leak_detection); build p85, native default/round trip/reopen persistence/OTR rejection pass, and the native fixture's net log shows a leak-check request attempted (DNS-blackholed) with the pref on and none with it off.

Last rebased: 2026-11-04 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
